<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <a href="/manage/checklists">Checklists</a> (under Rota in the menu) are the routines a location runs on some days,
        such as <strong>Opening</strong>, <strong>Closing</strong> or <strong>Party room reset</strong>. Each one is a list
        of tasks in the order they're done. Staff on shift tick the tasks off, and Lanyard records who ticked each one and
        when.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Who can do what">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Managers</strong> set up the checklists for the location they signed in to.</li>
            <li><strong>Admins</strong> can set them up for any location in the company, using the <strong>Location</strong>
                box at the top of the page.</li>
            <li>Staff never see the setup pages.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="What's kept">
        <ul>
            <li>Each day a checklist runs, Lanyard keeps a copy of its tasks as they were that day, so changing or removing
                a task later doesn't change past days.</li>
            <li>Archiving a checklist hides it from staff but keeps its history. <strong>Show archived</strong> lists it
                again, and <strong>Restore</strong> brings it back.</li>
            <li>Ticks are kept for six years, like clock-in records. If someone's account is deleted, their ticks stay
                but no longer show their name.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpNote>
        Checklists can be switched off for a company under Manage &gt; Companies &amp; Locations
        (<strong>Checklists</strong>). They also need <strong>Shift management</strong>, because the rota decides who can
        tick them.
    </HelpNote>
</HelpTab>
